#### Problem 1: Fragmented EDI Processing Across Product Teams

**Scenario**: Claims processing team and provider portal team both need 837 claim submission capabilities:

```csharp
// Product Team A: Gainwell Enterprise claims processing
public class ClaimsProcessor
{
    // Custom-built X12 837 parser
    public async Task<ClaimResult> ProcessInbound837Claim(Stream ediFile)
    {
        var x12Content = await ReadEdiFileAsync(ediFile);

        // Custom parsing logic (500+ lines)
        var claim = new Claim();
        var segments = x12Content.Split('~');

        foreach (var segment in segments)
        {
            if (segment.StartsWith(\"CLM\"))
            {
                // Parse CLM segment (claim information)
                var elements = segment.Split('*');
                claim.ClaimId = elements[1];
                claim.TotalChargeAmount = decimal.Parse(elements[2]);
                // ... 20+ more fields
            }
            else if (segment.StartsWith(\"NM1\"))
            {
                // Parse NM1 segment (name information)
                // Duplicated parsing logic across products
            }
            // ... 50+ segment types
        }

        // Custom validation logic
        if (!ValidateNpi(claim.BillingProviderNpi))
            throw new ValidationException(\"Invalid NPI\");

        return await SubmitClaimToAdjudication(claim);
    }
}

// Product Team B: Gainwell Provider+ portal (duplicate implementation)
public class ProviderClaimSubmissionService
{
    // Different custom X12 parser with subtle differences
    public async Task<SubmissionResult> SubmitProviderClaim(ClaimSubmission submission)
    {
        // Generate 837 EDI from JSON input (another 500+ lines)
        var x12Builder = new StringBuilder();
        x12Builder.Append(\"ISA*00*          *00*          *ZZ*SUBMITTER_ID   *ZZ*RECEIVER_ID    *\");
        x12Builder.Append(DateTime.Now.ToString(\"yyMMdd\"));
        x12Builder.Append(\"*\");
        x12Builder.Append(DateTime.Now.ToString(\"HHmm\"));
        // ... 200+ lines of manual X12 generation

        // Different validation rules than Team A
        if (submission.TotalCharges < 0)
            throw new InvalidOperationException(\"Negative charges not allowed\");

        return await SendToPayerAsync(x12Builder.ToString());
    }
}
```

**Problems**:
- **Code duplication**: Each product team implements X12 parsing/generation independently
- **Inconsistent validation**: Different teams enforce different rules (Team A validates NPI format, Team B checks charge amounts but not NPI)
- **Maintenance nightmare**: X12 standard updates require changes in 15+ repositories
- **Payer rejection rates**: Higher rejection rates due to inconsistent X12 formatting across products
- **Onboarding delays**: New trading partners require configuration changes in multiple systems (6-9 month integration cycles)

**Impact**:
- Support burden: Many tickets related to EDI format errors
- Payer dissatisfaction: Trading partners complain about inconsistent X12 formatting from same organization

